<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bato the Daesitiate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 6–<a href="/years/9">9 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Bato of the Daesitiates</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bato the Daesitiate was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daesitiates">Daesitiates</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and the principal commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-illyrian-revolt">Great Illyrian Revolt</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 6–9 CE. He fought alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bato-the-breucian">Bato the Breucian</a>, but had him executed in 8 CE for betraying the rising. After a long resistance he surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> in 9 CE and was sent into honourable exile at Ravenna.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bato-the-daesitiate.jpg" alt="Bato the Daesitiate" width="278" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LeonDardan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ilirski_bojevnik_-_Bato.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
